@@ -9348,3 +9348,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-19: PHASE D (CROSS-DOMAIN DETECTION CALIBRATION REPAIR; complementary; cached; verifier_is_oracle=false) -- SteerConf steered-confidence elicitation (arXiv:2503.02863) to rescue code_humaneval DETECTION where the .407 semantic-confidence-aggregation could not. .407 (exp4408) reported detection_calibrated_multi_domain=false: code_humaneval detection AUROC 0.577 (CI95 [0.46,0.69], n=539) -- AT CHANCE -- even after proper pools (n>=300) + semantic-confidence aggregation + base-rate separation, while FoVer detects at 0.918. The verifier is DOMAIN-BOUND. STATED forward difference (SteerConf, arXiv:2503.02863): add CONSERVATIVE/OPTIMISTIC steering probes + confidence-CONSISTENCY features (does the candidate's correctness signal survive a conservative vs optimistic steer?) BESIDE the verifier score, then fit domain-wise calibration with leave-domain-out + a random-score control -- testing whether STEERED confidence consistency rescues code_humaneval where the .407 static aggregation could not, WITHOUT degrading FoVer/GAP/GSM. Emit detection_calibrated_multi_domain BARE bool := (detection AUROC CI95 lower bound > 0.5 on >=2 NON-FoVer domains AND leave-one-domain-out calibration keeps ECE below the uncalibrated baseline on the held-out domain). verifier_is_oracle=false. A win = a deployable multi-domain detector contract (the verifier-domain-expansion step, north-star §0 step 2); a domain STILL at chance is LOGGED as a domain-bound missing-verifier gap. This is cross-domain DETECTION (AUROC), NOT the RETIRED cross-domain SELECTION axis (exp4314). Cached candidates, CPU, zero quota. NO new live inference (the steering probes are over CACHED candidate logits/scores where available, else cached candidate features); NO TRM training. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: clean_null_steered_confidence_does_not_rescue_code_detector; results/experiment_4419_steerconf_code_detection_calibration_repair.json
 - 2026-06-19: PHASE E1 (SOTA-ingestion; mandatory per SOTA-Ingestion Cycle Discipline) -- ingest the SOTA for the .408 bleeding-edge forks (verifier-grounded config-rule induction; Agent2World adaptive E3 world-model repair; the hidden-state localizer falsification; sovereign GAP-4 with a local generator; cross-domain detection calibration) and MAP the strongest 3-5 methods onto the .409 roadmap, CONDITIONED on the .408 outcomes (did verifier-grounded config-rule induction add reproducible levels? did Agent2World adaptive repair deepen the deep-tail? did the hidden-state audit find any off-text first-error signal or conclusively close the localizer? did a LOCAL generator hold the GAP-4 gate? did the config-rule vocabulary transfer? did SteerConf rescue code detection?). Use the RELIABLE channel ONLY (scripts/sweep_clusters.py / sweep_semscholar.py + low-concurrency WebSearch/WebFetch). Every method MUST carry a real, VERIFIED arXiv ID/URL (no citation = fabrication). FLAG any verifier-as-reward GENERATOR-training method (A2D2 2606.13565 / SEPO 2502.01384 class) as OUT-OF-BAND/operator-owned. Update research-studying.md (mark ingested) and emit flagged_for_v409 (the single strongest method for the .409 planner). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: sota_ingestion_v409_mapped; results/experiment_4420_sota_ingestion_v409.json
 - 2026-06-19: PHASE E2 (INFRA/HYGIENE) -- registry/gaps hygiene + GAP-4 regression guard. (1) Reconcile ops/verifier_registry.yaml + ops/verifier_gaps.md + ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml with the .408 outcomes: the verifier-grounded config-rule SOLVE (exp4414 -- new reproducible levels + grounded win-rules + the config-rule gaps); the Agent2World adaptive E3 repair (exp4415); the hidden-state localizer FALSIFICATION (exp4416 -- if it closed the first-error-localizer program, move GAP-FOVER-BIPRM-LOCALIZATION to a sharpened/closed off-text gap; if it found signal, log it); the sovereign GAP-4 result (exp4417 -- the decentralization tier); the config-rule vocabulary transfer (exp4418); the SteerConf calibration repair (exp4419 -- any still-at-chance domain as a domain-bound gap). (2) Run the GAP-4 execution regression guard (the ARC oracle-distinct verifier-beats-vote result must not silently regress). (3) Verify the capstone verifier_is_oracle stamping fix is STILL durable (confirm the .408 capstone path inherits it). Use the robust aggregate-available helper (read available artifacts, report gaps -- do NOT hard-block all-False if one is missing). Emit regression_guard_passed BARE bool. NO production verifier edits (audit-only per Verifier Authenticity Discipline). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: registry_gaps_reconciled_guard_passed; results/experiment_4421_registry_gaps_hygiene_gap4_guard.json
+- 2026-06-19: PHASE E3 (HARDWARE CONTINUITY; KV260 opportunistic per north-star §3) -- KV260 SSH-reachability + loaded-bitstream continuity check. Per north-star §3, KV260 is THE sovereignty story (drive to terminal, then freeze); GateMate/PolarFire are opportunistic-only. SSH-reachability precondition ONLY (NEVER a host SD-card precondition per KV260 SSH-Not-SD-Card Discipline). If the board is reachable, record the loaded overlay (xmutil listapps) + a lightweight liveness check (the carnot_ising bitstream UIO device present). If unreachable -> honest_verdict blocked_kv260_ssh_unreachable (a clean documented skip, NOT a fabrication). This keeps the board visible in the milestone retro without burning a deep task slot. NO host SD-card-device precondition (the retired mechanism). NO TRM training. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success_kv260_reachable_overlay_unknown; results/experiment_4422_hardware_continuity_kv260.json
